Kubernetes (K8s) is a platform used to manage containers.
It automates deploying, running, and scaling containerized applications.
A Pod is the smallest unit in Kubernetes.
A Deployment manages and maintains multiple Pods.
A Service provides network access to Pods.
Kubernetes can automatically restart failed containers.
It can scale applications by increasing or decreasing Pods.
A Cluster is a group of machines running Kubernetes.
Kubernetes uses YAML files to define application configurations.
Kubernetes helps applications be scalable, reliable, and highly available
